Ladybird now resumes a waiting resource selection from a media element
task, and drops the selector when a new load begins. Run in Chrome
157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5, none of the three
engines crashes when a source is appended to, or moved into, a waiting
video in a removed iframe’s document. Once such a video is adopted into
a fully active document, Firefox and WebKit load the source (or the src
set before adoption), as Ladybird now does; Chrome loads neither. And
when a wait ends in a fetch while the task from the waiting step is
still queued, Chrome and Firefox both keep that fetch delaying the load
event, as Ladybird now does.
